    "math_academy_id": "q-61907",
    "knowledge_point_id": "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d480892817efecf5ebea6860bece7cbae8127a9840e94ece34f9e83313abd5e5.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the cube above if it is $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?",
    "worked_solution": "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/efca24e18b188363ec3698ff4deaa5d5bd4ec1bdb5075138f925573a407c1f79.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=5\\times 5=25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 25 \\\\  & =150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
